{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_cluster_security", "label": "Cluster security", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "The cluster transport defaults to plain TCP without authentication; this page is the production hardening recipe for it.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_mutual_tls", "label": "Mutual TLS on the cluster transport", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A shared ca makes every connection require a peer certificate in both directions, addressing eavesdropping and unauthorized joins together. cert and key carry the material itself, never a path.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_certificate_address_binding", "label": "Certificate must vouch for the claimed address", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The hello frame carries an address and no credential, so a CA-signed node could announce another member's address; the CN or a SAN must cover the host or the full systemName@host, wildcards in the leftmost label only.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_request_client_cert", "label": "requestClientCert admission control", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Defaults to true whenever ca is present, since a trust bundle on a cluster listener has no other purpose; a listener that does not request one completes a handshake with any client, which may then claim any node identity.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_bind_time_refusals", "label": "Three configurations refused at bind time", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "An incomplete server credential, requestClientCert without ca, and an mTLS listener on Deno are refused rather than started in a weaker state than they read as. Empty counts as absent, which is what an unset env var looks like on arrival.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_incomplete_credential_downgrade", "label": "Incomplete credential silently bound plaintext", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "With only a cert or only a key the listener concluded no TLS and bound plaintext while the same options still dialled out over TLS, so the cluster formed and the node looked configured; a half-applied secret rotation was enough. It now throws at bind.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_deno_listener_limitation", "label": "Deno cannot host an mTLS listener", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Deno.listenTls takes only a cert and key with no way to request or verify a client certificate; a Deno node can still join by dialling out, so keep the seed nodes on Node.js or Bun.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_certificate_management", "label": "Certificate management approaches", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Self-signed for development only, a private CA for production so rotation stays per-node, cert-manager or Vault for Kubernetes with automatic renewal.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_network_policy", "label": "Firewalling the cluster port", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Even with TLS and auth, expose port 2552 narrowly; a NetworkPolicy limits it to pods carrying the app label so no Service or Ingress ever reaches it.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_threat_model", "label": "Cluster transport threat model", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Transport-level security only; application-level auth between actors and per-tenant isolation remain the operator's job, because the cluster transport is trusted within itself.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_pinned_addresses", "label": "pinnedAddresses on the seed provider", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A seed answer arrives before any certificate is checked; pinning bounds what a DNS or Endpoints compromise buys and is the only discovery-layer control left standing when mTLS is not in place.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_wire_frame_validation", "label": "Wire-edge frame validation", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Frames were cast to the protocol type rather than checked; null alone was an eight-byte remote process kill needing no completed handshake. A failed validation drops the frame and keeps the link, a throwing handler drops the connection.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_linear_decode_buffer", "label": "Linear decode buffer", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The decoder rebuilt its accumulator on every chunk, so a frame just under the 16 MiB cap in 1400-byte writes cost about 100 GB of copying - roughly 6000x amplification, reachable before the hello gate. Doubling growth makes it 1x.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_stall_deadline", "label": "Incomplete-frame stall deadline", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Thirty seconds without another byte, re-armed on every chunk: a stall bound rather than a budget for the frame, so a peer shipping a large frame over a congested link is never punished for being slow, only for going silent.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_handshake_deadline", "label": "Handshake deadline on accepted sockets", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Five seconds from accept, because a socket sending no bytes at all is not stalled mid-frame so nothing tracks it. On Bun the open callback fires before the TLS handshake, so a slot could be taken while there is still no certificate to check.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_inbound_connection_cap", "label": "Inbound connection cap of 1024", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Set far above any realistic full mesh; the newest connection is refused rather than an established one evicted, because eviction would let an attacker push real peers off the node.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_registry_caps", "label": "Per-registry growth caps", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A well-formed frame naming 100000 topics allocated 100000 map entries with no local Subscribe and no log line; members, tombstones, pub-sub and receptionist registries are now capped. Over-cap gossip is dropped and logged, a local Subscribe gets SubscribeRejected.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_tombstone_cap", "label": "Tombstone cap as the load-bearing membership cap", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A phantom live member is watched by the failure detector and dropped down-after seconds later, but a removed record is watched by nothing until the tombstone TTL a day later, so max-tombstones is the cap doing the work.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_bucket_charging", "label": "Caps charged on the bucket a record enters", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Charging only entry creation let the two caps trade headroom: a re-incarnation vacated the tombstone bucket without giving up a map slot, so alternating the two grew the map without bound while respecting both caps at every individual step.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_gossip_authority_rules", "label": "Gossip authority rules", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Nobody downgrades us, except leader promotion out of joining or weakly-up; third-party claims need a sender this node already considers active. Both key on the connection peer, not the payload from field, which the attacker fully controls.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_unreachability_exception", "label": "Unreachability deliberately left unrestricted", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "I cannot reach C is inherently a third-party observation and every node must converge on the same view before a downing provider decides; refusing those claims would leave each node with only its own reachability picture.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_sharding_directive_origin", "label": "Sharding directives need coordinator provenance", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A ShardRegion treated any sharding.* kind as a framework directive. It now claims its own envelope-router path to get the connection peer and wraps the frame in a class instance - a shape a JSON wire body cannot mint, unlike a tagged kind object.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_version_skew_cap", "label": "Gossip version skew cap", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Versions seed from Date.now, so an address could be claimed before the node owning it exists and the real owner then loses every merge. A five minute budget applies to every merge, because any rule letting a record earn a wider budget fails one step later.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_gossip_frame_sequence", "label": "Per-sender gossip frame sequence", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A captured frame stays valid because a member version only moves when its status does; replaying a downed member pre-down record revived it, roles included. A frame must out-number the highest sequence accepted from that connection peer.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_missing_incarnation_identity", "label": "Missing incarnation identity residual", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Two residuals remain: a fresh forged frame naming a deleted address at its old version, and a sequence mark that dies with its sender so an evicted pair can be replayed in capture order. Both need a restart to be a different member at the same host and port.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_reject_unauthorized_false", "label": "rejectUnauthorized false defeats authentication", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Tempting during debugging but it accepts any certificate; fix the certificate hostnames instead. Deno has no equivalent and always validates the chain, so reaching a self-signed peer means supplying its signing CA in ca.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_cluster_security", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_mutual_tls", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_cluster_security", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_certificate_address_binding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/cluster-security.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_cluster_security", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_cluster_security_reque